                <pb facs="0485" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.9111/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-29T22:00:00-05:00">December 29, 1941—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. Your 260, December 19, and 261, December 20. Although it is unlikely that
                    the Department would be able to fall in with this suggestion in its present
                    form, we shall be glad to study the matter, with a view to making such helpful
                    suggestions as may be possible, as soon as the text of the treaty is
                    received.</p>
                <p>In your discretion you may so inform the Iranian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
